<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramadan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramadan is the ninth month of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islamic-calendar">Islamic calendar</a>, observed by Muslims as a month of fasting, prayer and reflection. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> profile, it was towards the end of Ramadan in 1121 that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-tumart">Ibn Tumart</a> proclaimed himself the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a>. This declaration began the movement that founded the Almohad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramadan.jpg" alt="Ramadan" width="320" height="187" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gabby Canonizado from Dubai, United Arab Emirates · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Breaking_the_Fast_(2)_(27351979537).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
